{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>As white as snow.</b> It is the nature of tzara'at to be white — ״וְאִם בַּהֶרֶת לְבָנָה הִיא״ (Leviticus 13). In this sign too He hinted to him that he had spoken lashon ha-ra, in saying ״They will not believe me״; therefore He struck him with tzara'at, as Miriam was stricken for lashon ha-ra (Shabbat 96)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:25.930602769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}